        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">For most home gyms, buy REP's Old School iron plates</strong> if
            budget comes first, at about $2.16 a pound for a full set, or REP's urethane-coated
            Equalizers if you want quiet, odour-free plates with handles and can pay about $3.45. CAP's
            grip plates are the cheapest reputable option on Amazon, REP's USA-made Equalizer iron
            plates are the pick for US manufacture, and Titan's rubber-coated grip set sits in between.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, get Olympic 2-inch plates, weigh and pair them when they arrive, use
